                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00001         ********************************************************************
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00002         * SCF - NitrOS-9 Sequential Character File Manager
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00003         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00004         * This contains an added SetStat call to allow placing prearranged data
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00005         * into the keyboard buffer of ANY SCF related device.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00006         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00007         * Usage:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00008         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00009         * Entry: X = Pointer to the string
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00010         *        Y = Length of the string
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00011         *        A = Path number
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00012         *        B = SS.Fill ($A0) (syscall SETSTAT function call number)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00013         * NOTE: If high bit of Y is set, no carriage return will be appended to
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00014         *       the read buffer (used in Shellplus V2.2 history)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00015         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00016         * This also includes Kevin Darlings SCF Editor patches.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00017         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00018         * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00019         * Comment
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00020         * ------------------------------------------------------------------
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00021         *          1993/04/20  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00022         * V1.09:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00023         * - Speeded up L05CC (write char to device) routine by a few cycles
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00024         * - Slightly optimized Insert char.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00025         * - Move branch table so Read & ReadLn are 1 cycle faster each; fixed
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00026         *   SS.Fill so size is truncated @ 256 bytes.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00027         * - Added NO CR option to SS.Fill (for use with modified Shellplus V2.2
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00028         *   command history).
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00029         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00030         *          1993/04/21  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00031         * Slight speedup to some of ReadLn parsing, TFM's in Open/Close.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00032         * - More optimization to read/write driver calls
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00033         * - Got rid of branch table @ L05E3 for speed
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00034         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00035         *          1993/05/21  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00036         * V1.10:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00037         * Added Boisy Pitre's patch for non-sharable devices.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00038         * - Saved 4 cycles in routine @ L042B
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00039         * - Modified Boisy's routine to not pshs/puls B (saves 2 cycles).
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00040         * - Changed buffer prefill of CR's to save 1 byte.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00041         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00042         *          1993/07/27  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00043         * V1.11:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00044         * Changed a BRA to a LBRA to a straight LBRA in L0322.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00045         * - Optimized path option character routine @ L032C
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00046         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00047         *          1993/08/03  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00048         * Modified vector table @ L033F to save 1 cycle on PD.PSC
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00049         * - Sped up uppercase conversion checks for ReadLn & WritLn
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00050         * - Changed 2 BRA's to L02F9 to do an LBRA straight to L05F8 (ReadLn loop)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00051         * - Moved L0565 routine so Reprint line, Insert & Delete char (on ReadLn)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00052         *   are 1 cycle faster / char printed
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00053         * - Changed 2 references to L0420 to go straight to L0565
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00054         * - Sped up ReadLn loop by 2 or 3 cycles per char read
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00055         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00056         *          1993/09/21  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00057         * V1.12:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00058         * Sped up L0435 by 1 or 2 cycles (depending on branch)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00059         * - Changed LDD ,S to TFR X,D (saves 1 cycle) @ L04F1 (Write & WritLn)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00060         * - Modified L04F1 to use W without TFR (+1 byte, -3 cycles) (Write)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00061         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00062         *          1993/11/09  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00063         * Took LDX #0/LDU PD.BUF,y from L03B5 & merged in @ L028A, L02EF & L0381.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00064         * Also changed BEQ @ L03A5 to skip re-loading X with 0.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00065         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00066         *          1993/11/10  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00067         * Moved L04B2 routine to allow a couple of BSR's instead of LBSR's In READ.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00068         * - Moved driver call right into READ loop (should save 25 cycles/char read)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00069         * - Moved driver call right into L0565 (should save 12 cycles/char written on echo,
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00070         *   line editing, etc.)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00071         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00072         *          1993/11/26  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00073         * Moved L02FE (ReadLn parsing) to end where ReadLn routine is moved L03E2
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00074         * so Read loop would be optimized for it (read char from driver) instead of
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00075         * L042B (write filled buffer to caller).
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00076         * Changed LDA #C$NULL to CLRA.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00077         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00078         *          1993/12/01  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00079         * Modified device write call (L056F) to preserve Y as well, to cut down on
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00080         * PSHS/PULS.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00081         * - Changed L03E2 & L03DA to exit immediately if PD.DEV or PD.DV2 (depending
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00082         * on which routine) is empty (eliminated redundant LEAX ,X).
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00083         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00084         *          1994/05/31  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00085         * Attempted mode to L03F1 to eliminate LDW #D$READ, changed:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00086         *      LDX V$DRIV,x
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00087         *      ADDW M$Exec,x
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00088         *      JSR w,x
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00089         * to:
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00090         *      LDW V$DRIV,x
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00091         *      ADDW M$Exec,w
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00092         *      JSR D$READ,w
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00093         * Did same to L05C9 & L056F (should speed up each by 1 cycle)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00094         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00095         *          1994/06/07  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00096         * Attempted to modify all M$Exec calls to use new V$DRIVEX (REQUIRES NEW IOMAN)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00097         * - L01FA (Get/SetStat), L03F1 (Read), L05C9 (Write), L056F (Write)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00098         * - Changed L046A to use LDB V.BUSY,x...CMPB ,s...TFR B,A
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00099         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00100         *          1994/06/08  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00101         * Changed TST <PD.EKO,y in read loop (L02BC) to LDB PD.EKO,y
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00102         * - Changed LEAX 1,X to LDB #1/ABX @ L02C4
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00103         * - Changed LEAX >L033F,pc @ L032C to use < (8 bit) version
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00104         * - Modified L02E5 to use D instead of X, allowing TSTA, and faster exit on 0 byte
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00105         *   just BRAnching to L0453
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00106         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00107         *          1994/06/09  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00108         * Changed LEAX 1,X to LDB #1/ABX @ L053D, L05F8, L0312, L0351, L03B8
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00109         * - Changed to L0573: All TST's changed to LDB's
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00110         * - Changed Open/Create init to use LEAX,PC instead of BSR/PULS X
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00111         * - Changed TST PD.CNT,y to LDA PD.CNT,y @ close
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00112         * - Eliminated L010D, changed references to it to go to L0129
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00113         * - Eliminated useless LEAX ,X @ L0182, and changed BEQ @ L0182 to go to L012A
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00114         *   instead of L0129 (speeds CLOSE by 5 or 10 cycles)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00115         * - Moved L06B9 into L012B, eliminate BSR/RTS, plus
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00116         * - Changed TST V.TYPE,x to LDB V.TYPE,x
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00117         * - Moved L0624 to just before L05F8 to eliminate BRA L05F8 (ReadLn)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00118         * - Changed TST PD.EKO,y @ L0413 to LDB PD.EKO,y
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00119         * - Moved L0413-L0423 routines to later in code to allow short branches
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00120         * - As result of above, changed 6 LBxx to Bxx
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00121         * - Changed TST PD.MIN,y @ L04BB to LDA PD.MIN,y
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00122         * - Changed TST PD.RAW,y/TST PD.UPC,y @ L0523 to LDB's
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00123         * - Changed TST PD.ALF,y @ L052A to LDB
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00124         * - L053D: Moved TST PD.RAW,y to before LDA -1,u to speed up WRITE, changed it to LDB
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00125         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00126         *          1994/06/10  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00127         * Changed TST PD.ALF,y to LDB @ L052A
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00128         * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRA/STA V.WAKE,u @ L03F1 (Read)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00129         * - Changed CLR V.BUSY,u to CLRA/STA V.BUSY,u @ L045D
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00130         * - Changed CLR PD.MIN,y to CLRA/STA PD.MIN,y, moved before LDA P$ID,x @ L04A7
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00131         * - Changed CLR PD.RAW,y @ L04BB to STA PD.RAW, since A already 0 to get there
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00132         * - Changed CLR V.PAUS,u to CLRA/STA V.PAUS,u @ L05A2
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00133         * - Changed TST PD.RAW,y to LDA PD.RAW,y @ L05A2
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00134         * - Changed TST PD.ALF,y to LDA PD.ALF,y @ L05A2
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00135         * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRB/STB V.WAKE,u @ L05C9
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00136         * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRB/STB V.WAKE,u @ L056F
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00137         * - Changed TST PD.UPC,y to LDB PD.UPC,y @ L0322
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00138         * - Changed TST PD.DLO,y/TST PD.EKO,y to LDB's @ L03A5
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00139         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00140         *          1994/06/16  ???
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00141         * Changed TST PD.UPC,y to LDB PD.UPC,y @ L0322
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00142         * - Changed TST PD.BSO,y to LDB PD.BSO,y @ L03BF
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00143         * - Changed TST PD.EKO,y to LDB PD.EKO,y @ L03BF
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00144         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00145         *          2002/10/11  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00146         * Merged NitrOS-9 and TuneUp versions for single-source maintenance.  Note that
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00147         * the 6809 version of TuneUp never seemed to call GrfDrv directly to do fast screen
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00148         * writes (see note around g.done label).
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00149         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00150         *  16r2    2002/05/16  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00151         * Removed pshs/puls of b from sharable code segment for non-NitrOS-9 because it was
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00152         * not needed.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00153         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00154         *  16r3    2002/08/16  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00155         * Now uses V$DRIVEX.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00156         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00157         *  16r4    2004/07/12  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00158         * 6809 version now calls the FAST TEXT entry point of GrfDrv.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00159         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00160         *  17      2010/01/15  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00161         * Fix for bug described in Artifact 2932883 on SF
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00162         * Also added Level 1 conditionals for eventual backporting
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00163         
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00164         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00165         *  17      2010/01/15  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00166         * Handling of device exclusivity using the SHARE. bit has been rearchitected.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00167         * The '93 patch looked at the mode bytes in the descriptor and driver and
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00168         * determined that if both were set, then only one path would be allowed to
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00169         * be opened on the device at a time.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00170         * I now believe this is wrong.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00171         * The mode bytes in the device driver and descriptor are capability bytes.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00172         * They advertise what the device is capable of doing (READ, WRITE, etc) so
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00173         * the mode bytes alone do not convey action, but merely what is possible.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00174         * When the user calls I$Open on a device, he passes the desired mode byte
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00175         * in RegA and IOMan checks to make sure that all bits in that register are
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00176         * set in the mode bytes of the driver and descriptor.  So once we get into
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00177         * the Open call of this file manager, we know that all set bits in RegA are
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00178         * also set in the mode bytes of the driver and descriptor.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00179         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00180         * For SHARE., what we SHOULD be doing is checking the number of open paths
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00181         * on the device.  If the SHARE. bit is set in RegA, then we check if a path
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00182         * is already open and if so, return the E$DevBsy error.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00183         * Likewise, if SHARE. is not set in RegA, we check the path at the head of
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00184         * the open path list, and if ITS mode byte has the SHARE. bit set, we exit
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00185         * with E$DevBsy too.  The idea is that if the SHARE. bit is set on the newly
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00186         * opened path or an existing path, then there can "be only one."
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00187         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00188         *  18      2010/01/23  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00189         * SCF has successfully been backported to NitrOS-9 Level 1.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00190         * SCF now returns on carry set after calling SS.Open.  Prior to this
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00191         * change, SS.ComSt would be called right after SS.Open even if SS.Open
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00192         * failed. This caused misery with the scdwn driver wildcard feature.
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00193         *
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00194         * EOU Version 1.0.0
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00195         *          2022/08/01  LCB
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00196         * slight optimization in ReadLn chars when echo is turned on & a control
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00197         * code other than CR was received. Saves 2 bytes/3 cyc for that case (other
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00198         * chars no change. (L0418)
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00199         * 2 lbsr's changed to bsr's (both CPU's) - bsr L0403 in g.loop & bsr L0565 in L0634
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00200         
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00201                             nam       SCF
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00202                             ttl       NitrOS-9 Sequential Character File Manager
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00203         
                      (1/modules/scf.asm):00204                             IFP1
